From f4ee4bda9897e2e100adc5d0901cb4d060266f89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:16:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] rdna-boosts: block 10: slab, fusion dispatcher and
 async input ring

Re-based onto a691b2345: 8 conflicted files / 22 hunks, plus four clean-applied call
sites whose signatures moved.  The block resolves and builds, but on the re-based tree it
GPU page-faulted at -c 8192 on a plain dense 4B; this commit is the resolution plus the
four defects that debug turned up.  Three of them were silent delivery-code losses.

- mmid.cu (9 hunks): the delivery's per-occurrence compaction on upstream's tile_spec grid,
  as R01/R09 established.
- ggml-cuda.cu (3): upstream's batched set/get_tensor_n plus the delivery's
  ggml_cuda_peer_copy_staged declaration; ggml_cuda_should_fuse_mul_mat_q keeps upstream's
  NVFP4 scale params; the dispatcher moves to ggml-cuda-try-fuse.cu.
- mmq.cuh (2), mmvq.cu (2): include set and the per-shape J selection, both sides kept.
- llama-ext.h / llama-context.h/.cpp (3): both device-layer-input APIs (upstream's
  embd_row/llama_set_embeddings_layer_inp_dev and the delivery's F1 llama_lf_*), the
  GGML_FORCE_N_RS_SEQ diagnostic and upstream's !causal_attn clamp, the F1 lf_dev_rows
  inverse map plus upstream's embd_row event recording.
- tests/test-backend-ops.cpp (2): additive on both sides.

Finding and fix 1 (the fault): ggml_cuda_mul_mat_q_pair passed the pre-#31047 value for
what upstream renamed from `ncols_max` (a column COUNT the launcher divided by J) to `ntj`
(the J-tile count, consumed directly as grid.x).  The dense gate+up pair therefore launched
grid.x = ncols instead of ncols/J (512 vs 4 on the 4B FFN) and enumerated tiles past
src1_q8_1/dst -> page fault.  Both arms now derive ntj like the single-node path; the routed
arm also builds the per-arm tile_spec it was passing as nullptr (upstream's kernel reads
tile_spec[jt] whenever ids_dst is set) and uses upstream's ids convention nchannels_y = 1
with the experts in tile_spec.  Diagnostic route: GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_FUSION=1 was clean,
GGML_PAIR_OFF=1 was clean, and a temporary launch dump showed ntj=512 on exactly the pair
launches and ntj=4 everywhere else.

Finding and fix 2 (silent, silent on top of silent): the routed-compact MoE MMQ dispatch
was unreachable -- its gate tested args.nchannels_y, which upstream's ids convention sets to
1 (n_experts now live in nchannels_x) -- and behind that, the compact kernel still passed
process_tile's old `tile_y_max_j` (inclusive max) after upstream renamed it `tile_y_j_sup`
(exclusive count), so the first column-count fix alone produced garbage text.  Both fixed:
the compact path is reachable, bit-identical to the plain path, and +1.9% prefill
(3489 vs 3423 t/s, Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B Q4_K_M, 5256-token prompt, 2x2 reps).

Finding and fix 3 (the dispatcher merge, TODO #290): the interim two-dispatcher split kept
upstream's inline copy as a fallback, but that copy was not upstream's arms -- it was ~490
lines of upstream's dispatcher merged with STALE DUPLICATES of delivery arms
(ssm_conv_in, op_ssm_conv_l2_gatebeta, op_rms_norm_q8_1, add_softplus_mul, shexp_down_gate,
l2_norm_pair, gate_beta_verify).  One of them, the inline SSM conv-input fold, fired on
qwen35moe decode and produced text that diverges from the unfused chain (a state-carrying
path).  Resolved by reconciling into ONE dispatcher: every arm was audited against upstream
master; all but the DSV4 hyper-connection post are already owned by the delivery's
dispatcher (or its newer equivalent), so the DSV4 HC post arm is folded in at upstream's
position and ggml_cuda_try_fuse_legacy() is deleted, together with the superseded
ggml_cuda_match_moe_weighted_reduction matcher + struct + constexpr that only it used.

Validated (gfx1201, ROCm 10.1, VMM build): build green, no `<<<<<<<`; same-seed greedy text
on the dense 4B (1472ebdadd46), Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B (013d09f165a5) and 3-GPU -sm tensor
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q8_0 (90decf558d96) is identical across default / pair-off / routed-off /
fused-vs-unfused, so every fusion arm is bit-identical to the unfused chain on this tree;
gate-norm-rows-alias.sh green (180 fused, 0 declined, fused == chain f476efaac086);
test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT_ID 931/931.  Fusion is worth +26% decode on the 4B (87.4 vs
69.0 t/s) and +38% on the 35B-A3B tensor arm (80.5 vs 58.4).
